---
/**
 * /portfolio-tracker
 *
 * Angle: Investors, portfolio trackers, net worth focused users
 * Audience: People who want to track investments across multiple asset classes
 * Intent: "I want to see all my investments in one place"
 *
 * Target Keywords (High Volume):
 * - portfolio tracker (1K-10K)
 * - investment tracker (1K-10K)
 * - stock tracker (10K-100K)
 * - crypto tracker (1K-10K)
 * - net worth tracking (1K-10K)
 * - asset tracker (1K-10K)
 * - wealth tracker (1K-10K)
 */

import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { pages } from '@/data/pages';
import AngleHero from '@/components/AngleHero.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import FeatureList from '@/components/FeatureList.astro';
import CTABlock from '@/components/CTABlock.astro';
import SiblingLinks from '@/components/SiblingLinks.astro';

const meta = pages.portfolioTracker;
---

<Layout
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  canonical={`/${meta.slug}`}
>

  <AngleHero
    title="Live Multi-Asset Portfolio Tracking"
    subtitle="Track stocks, crypto, ETFs, commodities, forex, and more in one beautiful dashboard. Always see your networth and portfolio in real time"
    keyword="investment & portfolio tracker"
  />

  <div class="w-full overflow-x-clip -mt-52 md:-mt-[21.2rem] mb-0 relative z-10 flex justify-center">
    <div class="scale-[1.15] md:scale-100 origin-center w-max max-w-full md:w-[960px] md:max-w-none min-w-0 shrink-0">
      <img
        src={`/images/${meta.slug}/hero_light.png`}
        alt={meta.title}
        class="w-auto max-w-full md:w-full h-auto rounded-lg block dark:hidden"
      />
      <img
        src={`/images/${meta.slug}/hero_dark.png`}
        alt={meta.title}
        class="w-auto max-w-full md:w-full h-auto rounded-lg block hidden dark:block"
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 1: Contemporary investing (under hero) -->
  <Section
    heading="DIY-Investing done right"
    subheading="With great power comes great responsibility"
    align="center"
    bg="stone"
    class="mt-4 md:mt-0 !pt-14 md:!pt-10"
  >
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto space-y-4 text-center">
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        Modern investors have unprecedented access: stocks, ETFs, crypto, commodities, forex, futures, and more. You can build a multi-asset portfolio that would have been impossible a decade ago. But with wealth scattered across multiple platforms, how do you actually know if you're winning? Your crypto might be up 40%, but if you don't account for your underperforming ETFs, shrinking cash reserves, and that commodity position you forgot about, you have no idea what your real returns are.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 2: Stop Guessing. Start Knowing. (6 cards) -->
  <Section
    heading="Stop Guessing. Start Knowing."
    align="center"
    class="!pt-8 md:!pt-12"
  >
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <FeatureList
        columns={2}
        features={[
          { label: 'Every Asset Class', detail: 'Track stocks, crypto, ETFs, commodities, forex, and futures in one unified dashboard; no more juggling apps.' },
          { label: 'Visual Insights', detail: 'Transform complex portfolio data into beautiful Sankey diagrams, performance charts, and interactive analytics.' },
          { label: 'True Net Worth', detail: 'See your complete financial picture with real-time tracking of assets, investments, debts, and monthly growth.' },
          { label: 'Institutional-Grade Analytics', detail: 'Get risk-adjusted returns, annualized volatility, and ROI calculations. Professional metrics for every investor.' },
          { label: 'Smart Projections', detail: 'Forecast your financial future with data-driven predictions based on your actual performance and cash flow trends.' },
          { label: 'Budget Connected', detail: 'The only portfolio tracker that integrates with zero-based budgeting for complete financial clarity.' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 3: Portfolio Performance -->
  <Section
    heading="Track performance over time"
    bg="stone"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER — Suggested talking points:
      - Total returns (realized + unrealized gains)
      - Performance by asset class
      - Historical tracking
      - Cost basis and gain/loss calculations

      Keywords to weave in: portfolio performance, investment returns, portfolio analysis
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: See your total portfolio performance — realized gains from sales, unrealized gains from current holdings. Know exactly how your investments are doing.]
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: Break down performance by asset class. Is your crypto outperforming stocks? Are commodities dragging? See it clearly.]
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 4: Net Worth Tracking -->
  <Section
    heading="Your net worth, over time"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER — Suggested talking points:
      - Assets minus liabilities = net worth
      - Net worth timeline chart
      - Watch your trajectory over months and years
      - Include non-investment assets (cash, property)

      Keywords to weave in: net worth tracking, networth, wealth tracker, wealth management
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: Net worth = everything you own minus everything you owe. Finzen tracks this over time, showing your financial trajectory.]
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: The net worth timeline is one of the most motivating charts in personal finance. Watch it grow over months and years.]
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 5: Asset Allocation -->
  <Section
    heading="Visualize your allocation"
    bg="stone"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER — Suggested talking points:
      - Diversification breakdown by asset type
      - See if you're overweight in any area
      - Allocation changes over time
      - Rebalancing insights

      Keywords to weave in: asset allocation, portfolio allocation, portfolio breakdown
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <FeatureList
        columns={2}
        features={[
          { label: 'Allocation Breakdown', detail: '[COPY: Pie charts showing % in stocks, crypto, commodities, etc.]' },
          { label: 'Diversification Check', detail: '[COPY: See if you are too concentrated in any single asset or class]' },
          { label: 'Allocation Over Time', detail: '[COPY: Track how your allocation shifts as markets move]' },
          { label: 'Rebalancing Visibility', detail: '[COPY: Know when your portfolio drifts from target allocation]' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 6: Why No Broker Sync -->
  <Section
    heading="Privacy-first portfolio tracking"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER — Suggested talking points:
      - Why Finzen doesn't connect to brokers
      - Manual entry = you control what's tracked
      - Security through isolation
      - Your broker credentials stay with you

      Link to: Privacy-First Finance page
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: Finzen doesn't connect to your brokerage accounts. That's intentional. You enter your holdings manually — which means your broker credentials never leave your broker.]
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: This is a security boundary, not a limitation. Your financial data stays encrypted and isolated.]
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- Section 7: Combined with Budgeting -->
  <Section
    heading="Investments + budgeting in one app"
    bg="stone"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER — Suggested talking points:
      - Most portfolio trackers ignore budgeting
      - Finzen shows how your budget feeds your investments
      - Complete financial picture
      - Link to Budget & Expense Tracker page
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        [COPY: Portfolio trackers usually ignore budgeting. Budgeting apps usually ignore investments. Finzen does both — so you can see how your monthly budget feeds your long-term wealth building.]
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>


  <CTABlock
    heading="See your complete portfolio"
    subtext="Stocks, crypto, commodities, forex — all in one view. No broker connection required."
  />

  <SiblingLinks slugs={meta.siblings} />

</Layout>
